Scope
  * Milestone B: orbit/zoom/reset camera verified; HUD labels ignore mouse so empty-space
    drags reach the camera while buttons still consume taps.
  * Milestone C: the world reveals a distinct ward stone per Chapter 01 level, warms its
    ground, and shows Nox the companion on chapter completion; resume from a save restores
    exactly the matching revealed prefix.
  * Milestone D: per-face readiness readout — every face is named and shown as "solid" or
    "N shades", objective faces are marked, so the player can read puzzle mastery across the
    whole cube, not only the win condition.
  * Milestone E: the granted Rootweave Gauntlet now delivers its declared capability. Its
    "perceive.resonance" effect surfaces a HUD line naming faces one turn from settling
    (distinct==2); the capability is keyed off the effect slot and appears only while the item
    is equipped. Presentation only — it reads the same truth, it does not alter it.
  * capture_frames.gd preserves and restores the player save (it plays the chapter for real).
  * Milestone F: the large-text accessibility choice persists across launches in a separate
    settings file (user://craftcube_settings.json), loaded defensively so a missing or
    malformed file falls back to the default and can never reset progression.
  * Milestone G: progress is flushed to disk on the OS close/back request
    (NOTIFICATION_WM_CLOSE_REQUEST / WM_GO_BACK_REQUEST), so a session ended by the Android
    back gesture never loses progress. save_progress() is idempotent and test-isolatable.
  * Milestone H: reduced-motion accessibility choice, persisted with the large-text option; a
    turn under reduced motion still runs the real animated lifecycle (logic advances once on
    settle) and simply sweeps instantly.

Limitations: rendering on a virtual X server only. There is no physical Android device in
this environment, so this is NOT a device playtest; the APK is an artifact, not a store build.

